# tally 2.2 (CHANGES.md 2.2-7), L §2.3 `flowsx`, §5.14.3: `flows` has no conversion clause; a total converted
# movement by movement is a sum of a def keyed by the movement that rounds each at its day. In a rule, `in PLN`
# after flows(…) reads on as a membership test and the line stops at `at`, refused by the grammar. (Was
# L8_3_flows_mode_not_rounding, the converted flows' mode check, gone with the form.)
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

unit EUR: currency minor 0.01

input fx: num PLN/EUR

input day: date

input eamt: money EUR

place konto: accounts EUR lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..

move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on start_of(m)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to konto amount eamt

def c: money PLN at reader
  rule base = flows(konto, 2026-01) in PLN at fx half-up

ask b: c law 2026-01-01

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01
  fx = 4.3333
  day = 2026-02-10
  eamt = 1.00 EUR
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PARSE cannot parse: expected end of line, got at (m.tally:29)
